2. Given the heterogeneity in the urban cooperative sector, a four-tiered regulatory framework has been adopted to balance the spirit of mutuality and cooperation more prevalent in banks of smaller sizes and those with limited area of operation vis-à-vis the growth ambitions of the large-sized UCBs to spread their area of operation and undertake more complex business activities. Accordingly, the UCBs are categorized into the following four tiers for regulatory purposes:
Tier 1 - All unit UCBs and salary earners' UCBs (irrespective of deposit size), and all other UCBs having deposits up to ₹100 crore;
Tier 2 - UCBs with deposits of more than ₹100 crore and up to ₹1000 crore;
